{
  "_comment": "Reference manifest: the shape a Blender exporter emits. A torso root with an arm that waves through a 1-second loop. Build and view it with: demiurg-convert two-bone-wave.json -o wave.demiurg && demiurg wave.demiurg --shot pose.png --clip wave --time 250. Three conventions it demonstrates: (1) +Z points DOWN (voxlap, not Blender) -- the head sits at low z and the arm hangs toward high z, so an exporter has to flip the height axis; (2) a bone's mesh pivot IS its joint, and a child's 'joint' is measured from the PARENT's pivot, not from the parent grid's corner; (3) the clip's four keys are hand-picked extremes, whereas a real exporter samples the F-curves per frame, because the engine interpolates linearly between keys.",

